\label{lemma-purity-one-divisor-general}
Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $U \subset X$ be open and dense.
Let $Y \to U$ be a finite \'etale morphism. Assume
\begin{enumerate}
\item $Y$ is unramified over $X$ in codimension $1$, and
\item $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ is regular for all $x \in X \setminus U$.
\end{enumerate}
Then there exists a finite \'etale morphism $Y' \to X$
whose restriction to $U$ is $Y$.

